C MP+hb-no-visibility
"Message passing with a scoped release/acquire but NO availability/visibility
 operations. Genuine Vulkan (SPIR-V) source sketch:

   // producer
   x = 1;
   OpAtomicStore f, Device, Release, 1          // release, but write not 'made available'
   // consumer
   r0 = OpAtomicLoad f, Device, Acquire         // acquire, but x not 'made visible'
   r1 = x

 Vulkan splits ordering into THREE steps: happens-before, then AVAILABILITY (push
 the write out to a memory domain) and VISIBILITY (pull it into the reader). A bare
 release/acquire gives happens-before but, across a memory domain, NOT availability
 or visibility, so Vulkan still ALLOWS the stale read (1:r0=1, 1:r1=0) unless the
 program issues availability+visibility (e.g. memory_semantics with
 MakeAvailable/MakeVisible and the right storage-class/memory scope). OpenCL has no
 such split: a scoped acquire that synchronises also makes the released writes
 visible, so OpenCL FORBIDS this outcome. => Vulkan allows / OpenCL forbids.

 The reverse direction (OpenCL allows / Vulkan forbids) is feature-level too:
 OpenCL's scope set and all_svm_devices / fine-grained SVM atomics have no exact
 Vulkan counterpart. herd7 ships neither model; see README."
{ int x=0; int f=0; }
P0 (int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  *x = 1;
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_release);
}
P1 (int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_acquire);
  int r1 = *x;
}
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=0)
